 * PO-02D1A, PO-02D1A.1 and PO-02D1B verifiers freeze.
 *
 * PO-02D2 changes only Platform Owner files: the invitation flag (flags.ts, PLATFORM_INVITATIONS_ENABLED — default off,
 * exactly "true", only with the console flag), its error code (errors.ts), the platform.companies.invite permission
 * (guards.ts), the pending-invitation list's opt-in id (companies.ts — without it the rows are PO-02B's exactly), the
 * console strings, stylesheet and status table (revoked / accepted), an optional focus-return target for the console
 * dialog (platform-dialog.tsx — existing callers unchanged), the Companies and Dashboard pages (the working Invite control,
 * row actions and the history view only while the flag is on), and the two freeze verifiers (this layer's hooks). It adds
 * seven Platform Owner files: the invitation read model (invitations.ts), the mutation service (invitation-actions.ts),
 * its server actions, the dialogs, the history kit, the invitation detail page and its not-found. No customer route,
 * component, library, auth, session, registration, schema module, SQL or business file is in either list; nothing
 * implements invitation acceptance (PO-02D3).
 *
 * The rule for an approved change is the one C8, ACC-01, the LCP stage and PO-01A…PO-02D1B used: no re-baseline. Each
 * changed file's hunks are recorded here byte for byte, [1cbbbc1's text, PO-02D2's text]; undone, the file is PO-02D1B's
 * (1cbbbc1) to the byte (PO02D2_BASE_SHA), so every older pin keeps its strength. Each freeze verifier's PO-02D2 check
 * proves the hunks are each file's only change and the added files are exactly as recorded.
 *
 * Generated from the diff against PO02D2_BASE (each hunk widened with context until it is unique in both files, its
 * 1cbbbc1 form nowhere in PO-02D2's); changing a PO-02D2 file means regenerating this record, which is then part of the
 * change under review.
 */
